m_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** Under the Irish Collective Asset-management Vehicles Act 2015, only the **ICAV itself** is a body corporate with legal personality. Its sub-funds are **not** separate legal persons.\n\n**How segregated liability fits in:**\n- The Act imposes **statutory segregated liability** between sub-funds. Each sub-fund's assets may meet only that sub-fund's liabilities, not creditors of another sub-fund.\n- The ICAV contracts, sues and is sued **in respect of a specific sub-fund**. Set-off is permitted only within the same sub-fund.\n- Contracts include implied terms barring counterparties from claiming against other sub-funds' assets.\n- Each sub-fund keeps separate books and records.\n\n**Practical caveat:** Segregation derives from Irish statute, not separate personality. Courts elsewhere, such as where assets or counterparties are located, may not recognise it, so offering documents typically disclose this risk.\n\nUmbrella Irish plcs share this structure under the Companies Act 2014.","ttft_ms":809,"type":"result","duration_ms":3185,"uuid":"701ded37-a28a-4169-9b40-72fe0aaef6ec","ttft_stream_ms":595,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":595,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
